jaṭh-ara, 〈1.〉 a. hard;
 old (incorrect 🞄for jaraṭha);
 〈2.〉 (-ára), n. belly;
 womb;
 🞄cavity, interior, front of the body (opp. back): 🞄in. with oneʼs front;
 -agni, m. fire of the 🞄belly, i. e. of digestion.

jāṭhara, a. (ī) relating to the belly;
 🞄(with agni, m. digestive fire, hunger);
 m. son.
